{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788162164047,"sessionID":"ses_fa93b44b9ffexxMGVHbRXk1gY5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_c46f325b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/project-test1/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/project-test1/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Security Assessment — 2026-08-31 — Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit\n2: \n3: ## Context\n4: **Project:** CVEs Analytics — container-image vulnerability analytics platform\n5: **Language/framework:** Python (uv-managed), FastAPI/uvicorn\n6: **Purpose:** Scans Docker container images for CVEs, enriches findings with threat intelligence, computes Bayesian risk scores, and models attack paths through the cyber kill chain. Exposes a CLI (`cves-analytics`) and a REST API.\n7: **Deployment:** No deployment config found (no Dockerfile/compose/uwsgi/gunicorn/nginx/k8s/serverless in repo root). API runs via `uvicorn src.api.main:create_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`.\n8: **Ports/services:** HTTP :8000 (FastAPI/uvicorn, bound to 0.0.0.0); SQLite DB `analytics.db`.\n9: **Auth model:** none visible — no auth middleware, all `/api/*` endpoints appear unauthenticated.\n10: **Data stores:** SQLite (`analytics.db`), reference data cache directory (`data/`), upload directory (`uploads/`).\n11: **External integrations:** container image scanning (Docker images), external CVE/OSV data sources (referenced in pipeline).\n12: **Notes:** `CVE_DEBUG` env var (default `false`); API binds to `0.0.0.0` (all interfaces); SSE job status stream endpoint (`/api/stream/{job_id}`); file upload handling implied (`--upload-dir`/`uploads/`).\n13: \n14: ## Semgrep baseline\n15: Semgrep scanned 30 source files. Findings (ERROR/WARNING only, CWE-89 SQL Injection):\n16: \n17: | file:line | rule-name | severity |\n18: |---|---|---|\n19: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:78 | python.sqlalchemy.security.sqlalchemy-execute-raw-query | ERROR |\n20: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:78 | python.lang.security.audit.formatted-sql-query | WARNING |\n21: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:82 | python.sqlalchemy.security.sqlalchemy-execute-raw-query | ERROR |\n22: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:82 | python.lang.security.audit.formatted-sql-query | WARNING |\n23: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:85 | python.sqlalchemy.security.sqlalchemy-execute-raw-query | ERROR |\n24: | src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:85 | python.lang.security.audit.formatted-sql-query | WARNING |\n25: \n26: All 6 findings point at `duckdb_store.py` lines 78, 82, 85 (SQL string composition / `f`-string formatted query). Semgrep self-rated: confidence LOW, likelihood LOW, impact HIGH. No other files flagged.\n27: \n28: ## Dependency scan baseline\n29: Grype: 0 matches (no dependency vulnerabilities). SBOM available (`.security-output/sbom.cyclonedx.json`, 1.7 MB) — used in step 7. No DIFF_SCOPE.md present.\n30: \n31: ## Attack surface\n32: ### Entry points\n33: | # | Type | Location | Auth required | Description |\n34: |---|------|----------|---------------|-------------|\n35: | 1 | REST route | src/api/routers/profiles.py:43 (POST) | none | Create profile (unauthenticated) |\n36: | 2 | REST route | src/api/routers/profiles.py:68 (GET) | none | Get profile by id |\n37: | 3 | REST route | src/api/routers/profiles.py:91 (PATCH) | none | Update profile — profile_id parameter |\n38: | 4 | REST route | src/api/routers/profiles.py:126 (DELETE) | none | Delete profile by profile_id |\n39: | 5 | REST route | src/api/routers/scans.py:69 (POST) | none | Trigger scan — profile_id parameter |\n40: | 6 | REST route | src/api/routers/scans.py:149 (POST) | none | Generate scenario — profile_id; feeds yaml.load sink |\n41: | 7 | REST route | src/api/routers/scans.py:122 (GET) | none | Get scan details by run_id |\n42: | 8 | REST route | src/api/routers/stream.py:18 (GET) | none | SSE job status stream by job_id |\n43: | 9 | REST route | src/api/main.py:59 (GET) | none | Health check |\n44: | 10 | CLI (argparse) | src/cli/pipeline.py:20 | n/a | `cves-analytics` entry point; --profile, --images, --data-dir |\n45: \n46: ### Trust boundaries\n47: | # | Boundary | Location | Data type |\n48: |---|----------|----------|-----------|\n49: | 1 | Public API -> service layer | src/api/routers/*.py -> src/services/*.py | profile_id, run_id, job_id, image names |\n50: | 2 | Service -> DuckDB store | src/services/*.py -> src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:78 | SQL query with interpolated table name |\n51: | 3 | API generate-scenario -> simulation | src/api/routers/scans.py:150 -> src/simulation/scenario_generator.py:68 | user-supplied scenario config -> yaml.load |\n52: | 4 | CLI -> pipeline -> store | src/cli/pipeline.py -> DuckDBStore | profile/image args |\n53: \n54: ### Notes\n55: - No authentication/authorization middleware — all `/api/*` routes public.\n56: - Route path parameters (profile_id, run_id, job_id) flow into DuckDB `_execute()` (SQL sink) and scenario generation (yaml.load sink).\n57: - `_validate_table_name()` at duckdb_store.py:18 uses an allowlist regex `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$` invoked before every interpolated table name (write_table L73, read_table L99, table_exists L123); the only caller (pipeline.py:129) passes the HARDCODED name `\"findings\"` → SQL injection fully neutralized. No finding (ref: full mitigation = no finding).\n58: - `yaml.load(f)` at scenario_generator.py:68 and application_templates.py:79 both use `YAML(typ=\"safe\")` (ruamel.yaml safe loader) → safe deserialization, no CWE-502. `ScenarioGenerator()` is constructed with the default `config_path=\"config/services.yaml\"` (scans.py:159 / cli/pipeline.py:76), so no user-controlled path reaches the `open()` at _load_config L60. No path traversal.\n59: \n60: ## Attack paths\n61: - src/api/main.py:59 (create_app) -> lifespan() -> _get_duckdb_store() -> DuckDBStore -> ._execute() (4 hops) -> src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:78/82/85 [DuckDB SQL sink]\n62: - src/cli/pipeline.py (_run_cli) -> main() -> DuckDBStore -> ._execute() (3 hops) -> src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py:78 [DuckDB SQL sink]\n63: - src/api/routers/scans.py:150 (generate_scenario handler) -> ScenarioGenerator.generate_scenario -> yaml.load(f) at src/simulation/scenario_generator.py:68 [unsafe deserialization sink] — reachable by data flow though graphify returned no directed path.\n64: \n65: ## Dead code candidates\n66: - src/simulation/application_templates.py `_load_application_templates()` (yaml.load at L79) — no directed call path from any entry point in graph; reachable only via application_builder.py import. Flagged for reachability check in step 6.\n67: \n68: ## Scanned files\n69: 49 source files (excluded: tests/, .venv/, .git/, caches, egg-info, graphify-out, .security-output):\n70: \n71: src/__init__.py, src/api/__init__.py, src/api/dependencies.py, src/api/main.py,\n72: src/api/routers/__init__.py, src/api/routers/profiles.py, src/api/routers/scans.py,\n73: src/api/routers/stream.py, src/cli/__init__.py, src/cli/pipeline.py,\n74: src/core/__init__.py, src/core/attack/__init__.py, src/core/attack/kill_chain.py,\n75: src/core/models/__init__.py, src/core/risk/__init__.py, src/core/risk/bayesian_assessor.py,\n76: src/data/__init__.py, src/data/loaders/__init__.py, src/data/loaders/cvss_bt.py,\n77: src/data/loaders/cwe.py, src/data/loaders/epss.py, src/data/loaders/kev.py,\n78: src/data/stores/__init__.py, src/data/stores/duckdb_store.py,\n79: src/data/transformers/__init__.py, src/data/transformers/enricher.py,\n80: src/db/sqlite_models.py, src/services/__init__.py, src/services/analysis.py,\n81: src/services/enrichment.py, src/services/pipeline.py, src/services/scanner.py,\n82: src/simulation/__init__.py, src/simulation/application_builder.py,\n83: src/simulation/application_templates.py, src/simulation/control_probabilities.py,\n84: src/simulation/control_type_selector.py, src/simulation/control_types.py,\n85: src/simulation/scenario_config.py, src/simulation/scenario_generator.py,\n86: src/simulation/security_controls.py, src/simulation/system_simulator.py,\n87: src/utils/__init__.py, src/utils/config.py, src/utils/logging_config.py, hello.py\n88: \n89: \n90: ## Findings\n91: ### src/api/main.py:55, src/api/routers/profiles.py:43, src/api/routers/scans.py:74 — No authentication on network-exposed REST API (0.0.0.0:8000)\n92: **CWE:** CWE-306 Missing Authentication\n93: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n94: **Impact:** LOW\n95: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n96: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n97: **Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood MEDIUM = LOW ([reachability], none)\n98: \n99: **Data flow:**\n100: Source:     README.md:15,55 — API launched with `uvicorn ... --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000` (all network interfaces, external exposure).\n101: Transform:  src/api/main.py:55-57 — `create_app()` registers all routers with no auth middleware/dependency; only `Depends` is `session_dep` (SQLite session, src/api/dependencies.py:44) — no credential check anywhere.\n102: Sink:       src/api/routers/profiles.py:48 (create_profile) / src/api/routers/scans.py:74 (trigger_scan) — state-mutating endpoints accept requests with no credential check.\n103: \n104: ```python\n105: # src/api/main.py:55-57\n106: app.include_router(profiles_router.router, prefix=\"/api/profiles\")\n107: app.include_router(scans_router.router, prefix=\"/api/profiles\")\n108: app.include_router(stream_router.router, prefix=\"/api/stream\")\n109: ```\n110: \n111: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reaches the API on 0.0.0.0:8000. -> 2. POSTs to /api/profiles (create) or /api/profiles/{id}/scans (trigger scan) with no authentication. -> 3. Unauthenticated state mutation: profile tampering, scan-triggering (resource use), scenario generation.\n112: \n113: **Mitigations:** None. No auth middleware; all `/api/*` endpoints public.\n114: **Fix:** Add an authentication dependency (e.g., FastAPI `Depends()`) to state-mutating routes; enforce credential validation before handling requests.\n115: \n116: \n117: ## Dead code findings\n118: None. The dead-code candidate `src/simulation/application_templates.py::_load_application_templates()` (yaml.load at L79) uses `YAML(typ=\"safe\")` → no vulnerability. No finding.\n119: \n120: ## Test-only findings\n121: None. All flagged code (`scanner.py` image validation, `sqlite_models.py` ORM, `profiles.py` pydantic) is exercised only under unit tests; no finding.\n122: \n123: ## Dependency findings\n124: - Grype: 0 matches.\n125: - OSV-Scanner: no issues found.\n126: - SBOM: present (`.security-output/sbom.cyclonedx.json`); no flagged CVEs.\n127: No dependency vulnerabilities found.\n128: \n129: \n130: ## Findings summary\n131: ### Findings table\n132: | file:line | CWE | Reachability | Impact | Likelihood | Confidence | Severity |\n133: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n134: | src/api/main.py:55, src/api/routers/profiles.py:43, src/api/routers/scans.py:74 | CWE-306 Missing Authentication | ACTIVE | LOW | MEDIUM | CONFIRMED | LOW |\n135: \n136: ### Severity summary\n137: | Severity | Count |\n138: |---|---|\n139: | CRITICAL | 0 |\n140: | HIGH | 0 |\n141: | MEDIUM | 0 |\n142: | LOW | 1 |\n143: \n144: ### Confidence summary\n145: | Confidence | Count |\n146: |---|---|\n147: | CONFIRMED | 1 |\n148: | PROBABLE | 0 |\n149: | LIKELY | 0 |\n150: | POSSIBLE | 0 |\n151: | UNLIKELY | 0 |\n152: \n153: ### Reachability summary\n154: | Reachability | Count |\n155: |---|---|\n156: | ACTIVE | 1 |\n157: | CONDITIONAL | 0 |\n158: | DEAD | 0 |\n159: \n160: ### Likelihood summary\n161: | Likelihood | Count |\n162: |---|---|\n163: | HIGH | 0 |\n164: | MEDIUM | 1 |\n165: | LOW | 0 |\n166: \n167: ### Impact summary\n168: | Impact | Count |\n169: |---|---|\n170: | CRITICAL | 0 |\n171: | HIGH | 0 |\n172: | MODERATE | 0 |\n173: | LOW | 1 |\n174: \n175: \n176: \n\n(End of file - total 176 lines)\n</content>","metadata"